{"header":{"status":{"name":"Success","code":0,"description":"Query success","apiHelp":"https://www.censtatd.gov.hk/en/web_table.html?id=315-37001&api_popup=1"},"title":"Balance of Payments (BoP)","tablenote":["Figures may not add up to the total due to rounding.     A positive value for the balance figure in the current account or the capital account represents a surplus whereas a negative value represents a deficit.     A new sign convention has been adopted for the entire series of the financial account since June 2023. From then on, an increase in assets/liabilities is indicated by a positive value. Note that an increase in assets indicates a net financial outflow, while an increase in liabilities indicates a net financial inflow. Therefore, an increase in the financial account balance (i.e. when assets minus liabilities is a positive value) indicates a net financial outflow.     The estimates of reserve and non-reserve assets under the Balance of Payments framework are transaction figures. Effects of valuation changes (including price changes and exchange rate changes) and reclassifications are not taken into account.","@ Figure is subject to revision later on."],"source":"Balance of Payments Branch (1),  Census and Statistics Department  (Enquiry telephone no. : 3863 2329  Enquiry e-mail : bop@censtatd.gov.hk)","count":{"noOfRecords":61,"started":"2026-10-20T20:02:02+00:00","finished":"2026-10-20T20:02:02+00:00","durationSeconds":0.087706}},"dataSet":[{"BOP_COMPONENT":"BOP_C","BOP_COMPONENTDesc":"Overall Balance of Payments","freq":"Y","period":"1998","sv":"BOP","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":-40165,"sd_value":""},{"BOP_COMPONENT":"CPA","BOP_COMPONENTDesc":"Capital account","freq":"Y","period":"1998","sv":"BOP","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":-38,"sd_value":""},{"BOP_COMPONENT":"CRA","BOP_COMPONENTDesc":"Current account","freq":"Y","period":"1998","sv":"BOP","svDesc":"HK$ million","figure":22226,"sd_value":""},{"BOP_COMPONENT":"DI","BOP_COMPONENTDesc":"Direct